-- p(X) :- q(X), \+ p(X). ;;q(a).
refused1.dl:1: p/1 is negated through its own recursion: no order to compute it in
-- p(X, Y) :- q(X). ;;q(a).
refused2.dl:1: the variable Y of the head is in no positive atom of the body
-- p(X) :- q(X), \+ r(Y). ;;q(a). ;;r(b).
refused3.dl:1: the variable Y of a negation is in no positive atom of the body
-- p(X) :- q(X), X < Y. ;;q(a).
refused4.dl:1: the variable Y of a comparison is in no positive atom of the body
-- p(f(a)).
refused5.dl:1: a compound term is not Datalog's: f(a)
-- p(X).
refused6.dl:1: a fact with a variable: p(_G1)
-- p(a) :- q(a ;;q(a).
refused7.dl:2: ) is expected, not q
-- p(X) :- q(X), nope(X). ;;q(a). ;;?- p(X).
warning: nope/1 has no fact and no rule
